// "Shuffle your graveyard into your library." — the graveyard-hate family's
// nullary composition ([CR#701.24a] shuffle; [CR#400.7] zone change): every
// card in your graveyard moves to your library, THEN the library shuffles —
// the shuffle must see the moved cards, so it runs second. Not a primitive
// verb: an `Each` distribution over the
// your-graveyard filter (`graveyard_card_filter`'s shape, migrations
// effect.rs — owned, not the any-graveyard exile family's owner-agnostic
// twin) feeding `Move(It, Library(FromTop(0)))` — a library destination is
// anchor-mandatory (a bare `Library` variant doesn't exist), and the anchor
// is irrelevant here since the very next step destroys all order. No
// `Composite` wrapper: "shuffle X into Y" is plain English, not a printed
// CR#701 keyword-action verb, so there is no "whenever you ~" event to name.
//
// Template: the whole nullary phrase, matching the effect-clause parser's
// `parse_macro_effect` "OneShotEffect" bare-emittable fallthrough
// (migrations effect.rs) — no slots, so it graduates and renders without any
// bespoke parser/render code of its own.
(
    name: "ShuffleYourGraveyardIntoLibrary",
    template: "shuffle your graveyard into your library",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    body: Sequentially([
        Each(
            binder: Existing(SelectAll(And([InZone(Graveyard), Owner(Ref(You))]))),
            effect: Move(It, Library(FromTop(0))),
        ),
        Shuffle,
    ]),
)
